    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Access-Services-Librarian---Faculty_R-097876": {
      "title": "Assistant Librarian, Access Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Librarian, Access Services Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department Library Services Proposed Minimum Salary $4,839.42 monthly Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Access Services Librarian will coordinate daily circulation services, including tracking course reserves, documenting user borrowing standards, and facilitating collection access for onsite and digital users. Additional duties will include individualized instruction at the reference desk, service through academic or library committees, and adherence to faculty librarian scholarship standards. The librarian may oversee a small number of part-time staff or student worker direct reports and complete basic administrative tasks. A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H‑1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University–Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H‑1B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Responsibilities : Manage to 2-4 part-time employees in access services. Create access services schedules for the Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Provide training for circulation services, including item lending, lamination, comb binding, printing, scanning, and other related tasks. Develop access services policies and procedures. Maintain collection statistics for common access services, such as annual lending, gate counts, and request types. Maintain circulation policy and permission settings in the Alma LMS. Staff the reference desk for 8 to 12 hours per week, split across two or more shifts, including one weekday evening. Develop collections in assigned subject fields that could include biology, chemistry, criminal justice, sociology, business, or other areas, depending on skill set and in partnership with faculty. Manage and coordinate library displays. Assist with library outreach and marketing, as needed, to help the department connect with campus and community members. Events may take place on or off campus. Assist with library instruction or public service events, as needed. Faculty Research and Service: Serves as a member of committees in the library and the university.  Remains current in the library discipline and assigned liaison areas. Publishes chapters, book reviews, or other peer-reviewed written content for theoretical or practical aspects of the library field. Participates in conferences and professional organizations. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Ability to design a variety of online and in-person general and subject-specific instruction sessions. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Effective interpersonal and customer service skills. Strong critical thinking, problem-solving, organizational, and decision-making skills.    Minimum Qualifications A Master of Library Science (MLS) degree, Master of Library and Information Science (MLIS) degree, or another equivalent from an American Library Association (ALA)-accredited university or college. Must be self-motivated, creative, and innovative with excellent interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Second master’s degree, with a preference for the hard sciences, computer science, social sciences, or business. A bachelor’s degree in the hard sciences, computer science, social sciences, or business. Two years of experience in a library, with a preference for academic libraries. Experience working in access services or an adjacent role at a library, with more weight given for two or more years of access services experience.   Experience managing employees, especially student workers or part-time library employees. More weight will be given for management in the context of access services. Experience providing library instruction. Experience working in reference at an academic library. Experience managing circulation policy and permission settings in the library's ILS (Alma) or a similar ILS.                                        Salary: $ 58,073.00 Hours: Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, and Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.; Wednesday from 12:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. Supervision of Others: This position may supervise other employees. Work Location: This is not a remote position. The selected candidate will be required to work on campus.   To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Applicants should submit a cover letter, résumé, and contact information for three professional references. Transcripts should be uploaded in the attachment section of the application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Management-Strategy_R-097888-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management/Strategy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Management/Strategy Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College of Business Administration Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Business Administration (COBA) at Texas A&M University-Central Texas welcomes highly qualified applicants to fill an immediate need for an Assistant or Associate Professor in Management / Strategy starting in Fall 2027. This is a tenure-track faculty position. Application reviews will begin immediately. We are looking for a dynamic and collegial teacher-scholar with a passion for teaching and a multi-faceted track record of excellence both within and beyond the classroom. Our greatest and immediate teaching need is for our undergraduate business strategy capstone course. Our hope is that this faculty member will deliver our capstone strategy course in such a way that students complete their undergraduate business programs on a high note. Courses in other related areas may also be available on a limited basis depending on applicant qualifications and interest. About Texas A&M University – Central Texas Established as an independent member of the Texas A&M University System in 2009, A&M-Central Texas is a friendly and dynamic regional teaching institution that prides itself on excellence in instruction, but also embraces a growing emphasis on research.  A&M-Central Texas is truly unique in that it is an upper- and masters-level institution, offering only junior- and senior-level coursework needed to successfully complete baccalaureate degrees and all coursework leading to the completion of master’s degrees.  As such, A&M-Central Texas maintains active partnerships with the major community colleges within the Austin and Central Texas region, as well with Fort Hood, a premier outpost of the U.S. Army and one of the largest military installations in the world.  Our multifaceted student demographic includes a significant proportion of first-generation college students, non-traditional learners, and military-affiliated personnel.    The College of Business Administration is accredited by AACSB, and we are eager to have dynamic and collegial new faculty members partner with us in pursuit of our major strategic initiatives, of which there are many on the near horizon (most notably, a DBA program anticipated to launch Fall 2027 pending SACSCOC final approval).  This is an exciting time of rapid change within the College that affords new faculty members many opportunities to make an immediate, significant, and lasting impact.   A&M-Central Texas is located on the southern edge of Killeen, TX, a city of approximately 150,000 located about halfway between Austin and Waco—about 60 miles either way.  Our faculty members enjoy a wide variety of living options by virtue of the culture in the area—from quiet and rural to bustling and cosmopolitan.  It is an easy drive to great art, food, shopping, and night life as well as to hunting, fishing, hiking, and camping for those who prefer the outdoors.  Central Texas is also a great place for families, with many options for schooling, worship, civic engagement, and recreation.  It also has light traffic and a reasonable cost of living.  The major metropolitan areas of Houston, Dallas-Fort Worth, and San Antonio are all within a 3-hour radius of Killeen.    Responsibilities The candidate will be expected to provide quality, engaging instruction for typically three courses of undergraduate business strategy per term, primarily at the undergraduate level and in a variety of course delivery formats (face-to-face, online, or hybrid), with fully online being the most in-demand option at present.  Summer teaching opportunities may also available as dictated by student demand and department needs.    Some scholarly contributions are also required.  The candidate is expected have sufficient scholarly and/or professional activities to have “scholarly academic” status upon arrival per AACSB faculty classifications, and to have a healthy pipeline of works in progress, where health is measured more by viability and impact than by volume.  Scholarship is but one category of currency and impact with which faculty may engage: others include maintaining a recognized professional certification, presenting at academic conferences, engaging in consulting or other industry-related activities, and completing other relevant professional training and development activities.  Professional development funds are available to support all of these endeavors, and faculty within the College frequently collaborate on research projects together.    In regard to service, faculty are expected to support the department, college, and university with committee work, but first-year faculty are exempt from this.  In addition, faculty are expected to have some sort of service to their profession and/or to the community, but again, service contribution impact and quality are more important than the numbers of activities engaged in.  Faculty generally have a lot of discretion in determining how best they can add value through their various service activities.  A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H‑1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University–Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H‑1B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Minimum Qualifications: To be eligible to apply for this position, candidates should: Possess a terminal degree (doctorate) in strategic management or a closely-related discipline from a regionally accredited university Be eligible for the AACSB “scholarly academic” faculty classification Have a documented track record of successfully teaching business strategy, including in fully online formats   Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate for this position would also possess: At least three (3) years of full-time collegiate teaching experience Experience working with doctoral students Industry experience, including ongoing connections Proficiency in creating original, dynamic, and engaging online course instructional materials Great administrative, organizational, and interpersonal skills to support successful instruction to a largely non-traditional, first-generation, and military-affiliated student body     Salary: Commensurate Hours: Faculty hours; M-F; hours may vary by assignment and course modality. To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Applicants are required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), and either the contact information for three professional references or three letters of recommendation. Additional materials, such as a teaching philosophy statement and transcripts, are optional but strongly encouraged. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Adjunct-Faculty---Marriage---Family-Therapy_R-083523-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Marriage & Family Therapy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty - Marriage & Family Therapy Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College Of Education and Human Development Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Applications for part-time adjunct faculty positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed when openings become available. Future teaching assignments are on a semester-by-semester basis, which may include fall, spring and summer.  The Marriage and Family Therapy Program within the Department of Counseling and Psychology at Texas A&M University – Central Texas is seeking applicants for adjunct instructors. The successful candidate(s) will be expected to teach graduate course either in person or online in the marriage and family therapy program. Experience and enthusiasm for teaching and working with graduate students is essential. A Ph.D. in Marriage and Family Therapy or related field is required. Applicants must also have a clear MFT identity (e.g. membership in professional associations, research, presentations, clinical practice) Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, graduate transcripts, and three professional letters of reference. Primarily responsible for the teaching/learning process. Adjunct instructors are hired to teach on a temporary and part-time basis. Adjunct instructors teaching courses for credit must meet the same requirements for professional and scholarly preparation as their full-time counterparts teaching in the same discipline. Disclosure: A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H‑1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University–Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H‑1B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Experience in clinical practice or instruction related to marriage and family therapy Exhibit enthusiasm for graduate teaching and employing innovative teaching methods. Minimum Qualifications : Ph.D. in Marriage and Family Therapy or related field Preferred Qualifications: MFT Doctoral Degree from COAMFTE accredited program AAMFT clinical membership and Approved Supervisor designation. To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Applicants are required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), graduate transcripts, and either the contact information for three professional references or three letters of recommendation. Completed employment application material must include: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Graduate Transcripts At least 3 Professional references or letters of reference All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Management-Leadership_R-097771": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management/Leadership",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Management/Leadership Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College of Business Administration Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Business Administration (COBA) at Texas A&M University-Central Texas welcomes highly qualified applicants to fill an immediate need for an Assistant Professor in Management / Leadership starting in Fall 2027.  This is a tenure-track faculty position.  Application reviews will begin immediately.  We are looking for a dynamic and collegial teacher-scholar with a passion for teaching and a multi-faceted track record of excellence both within and beyond the classroom.  This faculty member would be expected to teach leadership-related courses at a variety of levels and in a variety of modalities.  Assigned courses will include undergraduate leadership and one or more of the following graduate courses: organization development and change (masters), cross-sector partnerships (masters), global leadership theory and practice (masters), leadership formation and development (masters), and any one of the in-development doctoral courses that would support our DBA leadership emphasis area (still pending final SACSCOC approval).  Other courses may also be available on a limited basis depending on applicant qualifications and interest.    While this position is being advertised at the rank of Assistant Professor, we warmly welcome applications from candidates with distinguished records and broader experience.  Depending on institutional needs and individual qualifications, consideration may be given for credit toward years of service and/or appointment at the rank of Associate Professor.  Please note that tenure upon hire is possible but atypical and is determined on a case-by-case basis in consultation with the Provost.   About Texas A&M University – Central Texas Established as an independent member of the Texas A&M University System in 2009, A&M-Central Texas is a friendly and dynamic regional teaching institution that prides itself on excellence in instruction, but also embraces a growing emphasis on research.  A&M-Central Texas is truly unique in that it is an upper- and masters-level institution, offering only junior- and senior-level coursework needed to successfully complete baccalaureate degrees and all coursework leading to the completion of master’s degrees.  As such, A&M-Central Texas maintains active partnerships with the major community colleges within the Austin and Central Texas region, as well with Fort Hood, a premier outpost of the U.S. Army and one of the largest military installations in the world.  Our multifaceted student demographic includes a significant proportion of first-generation college students, non-traditional learners, and military-affiliated personnel.    The College of Business Administration is accredited by AACSB, and we are eager to have dynamic and collegial new faculty members partner with us in pursuit of our major strategic initiatives, of which there are many on the near horizon (most notably, a DBA program anticipated to launch Fall 2027 pending SACSCOC final approval).  This is an exciting time of rapid change within the College that affords new faculty members many opportunities to make an immediate, significant, and lasting impact.   A&M-Central Texas is located on the southern edge of Killeen, TX, a city of approximately 150,000 located about halfway between Austin and Waco—about 60 miles either way.  Our faculty members enjoy a wide variety of living options by virtue of the culture in the area—from quiet and rural to bustling and cosmopolitan.  It is an easy drive to great art, food, shopping, and night life as well as to hunting, fishing, hiking, and camping for those who prefer the outdoors.  Central Texas is also a great place for families, with many options for schooling, worship, civic engagement, and recreation.  It also has light traffic and a reasonable cost of living.  The major metropolitan areas of Houston, Dallas-Fort Worth, and San Antonio are all within a 3-hour radius of Killeen.    Responsibilities The candidate will be expected to provide quality, engaging instruction for typically three courses per long term in a variety of course delivery formats (face-to-face, online, or hybrid), with fully online being the most in-demand option at present.  Summer teaching opportunities may also available as dictated by student demand and department needs.  Some scholarly contributions are also required.  The candidate is expected have sufficient scholarly and/or professional activities to have “scholarly academic” status upon arrival per AACSB faculty classifications, and to have a healthy pipeline of works in progress, where health is measured more by viability and impact than by volume.  Scholarship is but one category of currency and impact with which faculty may engage: others include maintaining a recognized professional certification, presenting at academic conferences, engaging in consulting or other industry-related activities, and completing other relevant professional training and development activities.  Professional development funds are available to support all of these endeavors, and faculty within the College frequently collaborate on research projects together.    In regard to service, faculty are expected to support the department, college, and university with committee work, but first-year faculty are exempt from this.  In addition, faculty are expected to have some sort of service to their profession and/or to the community, but again, service contribution impact and quality are more important than the number of activities engaged in.  Faculty (in consultation with the department chair) generally have a lot of discretion in determining how best they can add value through their various service activities.  A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H‑1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University–Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H‑1B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer.   Minimum Qualifications: To be eligible to apply for this position, candidates should: Possess a terminal degree (doctorate) in management / leadership or a closely-related discipline from a regionally accredited university Be eligible for the AACSB “scholarly academic” faculty classification Have a documented track record of successfully teaching leadership courses, including in fully online formats   Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate for this position would also possess: At least three (3) years of full-time collegiate teaching experience Experience working with doctoral students Industry experience, including ongoing connections Proficiency in creating original, dynamic, and engaging online course instructional materials Great administrative, organizational, and interpersonal skills to support successful instruction to a largely non-traditional, first-generation, and military-affiliated student body Salary: Commensurate Hours: Faculty hours; M-F; hours may vary by assignment and course modality. To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Applicants are required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), and either the contact information for three professional references or three letters of recommendation. Additional materials, such as a teaching philosophy statement and transcripts, are optional but strongly encouraged. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Supply-Chain-Management_R-097482-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College of Business Administration Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Business Administration (COBA) at Texas A&M University-Central Texas welcomes highly qualified applicants to fill an immediate need for an Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management starting in Fall 2027.  This is a tenure-track faculty position.  Application reviews will begin immediately.  We are looking for a collegial teacher-scholar with a passion for teaching and a multi-faceted track record of excellence both within and beyond the classroom.  Our greatest and immediate teaching need is for undergraduate courses in support of our brand-new BBA in Logistics & Supply Chain Management program.  Our hope is that this faculty member will help establish this as a strong program with great student outcomes and robust regional industry connections.  Courses at other levels and in other related areas may also be available on a limited basis depending on applicant qualifications and interest.    About Texas A&M University – Central Texas Established as an independent member of the Texas A&M University System in 2009, A&M-Central Texas is a friendly and dynamic regional teaching institution that prides itself on excellence in instruction but also embraces a growing emphasis on research.  A&M-Central Texas is truly unique in that it is an upper- and masters-level institution, offering only junior- and senior-level coursework needed to successfully complete baccalaureate degrees and all coursework leading to the completion of master’s degrees.  As such, A&M-Central Texas maintains active partnerships with the major community colleges within the Greater Austin and Central Texas regions, as well as with Fort Hood, a premier outpost of the U.S. Army and one of the largest military installations in the world.  Our multifaceted student demographic includes a significant proportion of first-generation college students, non-traditional learners, and military-affiliated personnel.    The College of Business Administration is accredited by AACSB, and we are eager to have energetic and collegial new faculty members partner with us in pursuit of our major strategic initiatives, of which there are many on the near horizon (most notably, a DBA program anticipated to launch Fall 2027 pending SACSCOC final approval).  This is an exciting time of rapid change within the University and College that affords new faculty members many opportunities to make an immediate, significant, and lasting impact.   A&M-Central Texas is located on the southern edge of Killeen, TX, a city of approximately 150,000 located about halfway between Austin and Waco—about 60 miles either way.  Our faculty members enjoy a wide variety of living options by virtue of the range of communities in the area—from quiet and rural to bustling and cosmopolitan.  It is an easy drive to great art, food, shopping, and night life as well as to hunting, fishing, hiking, and camping for those who prefer the outdoors.  Central Texas is a rapidly growing region with a booming economy, but is also a great place for families, with many options for schooling, worship, civic engagement, and recreation.  It also has modest traffic and a reasonable cost of living.  The major metropolitan areas of Houston, Dallas-Fort Worth, and San Antonio are all within a 3-hour radius of Killeen.  Responsibilities: The candidate will be expected to provide quality, engaging instruction for typically three courses per term, primarily at the undergraduate level and in a variety of course delivery formats (face-to-face, online, or hybrid), with fully online being the most in-demand option at present.  Candidates who possess exceptional skill at making technical content accessible to a broad audience are especially desired.  The candidate will be expected to teach the following courses: LSCM 4321 Production and Operations Management, LSCM 4322 Business Process, Quality, and Lean Management, LSCM 4326 Global Procurement and Strategic Sourcing.  Other assigned courses may include LSCM 4323 Supply Chain Management and BUSI 3311 Business Statistics.  Additional summer teaching opportunities may be available depending on student demand and department needs.  Some scholarly contributions are also required.  The candidate is expected have sufficient scholarly and/or professional activities to have “scholarly academic” status upon arrival per AACSB faculty classifications, and to have a healthy pipeline of works in progress toward publication, where health is measured more by viability and anticipated impact than by number and/or status.  Scholarship is but one category of currency and impact with which faculty may engage: others include maintaining a recognized professional certification, presenting at academic conferences, engaging in consulting or other industry-related activities, and completing other relevant professional training and development activities.  Professional development funds are available to support all of these endeavors, and faculty within the College frequently collaborate on research projects together.    In regard to service, faculty are expected to support their program(s), department, college, and/or university with committee work, but first-year faculty are exempt from this.  In addition, faculty are expected to have some sort of service to their profession and/or to the community, but again, service contribution impact and quality are more important than the numbers of activities engaged in.  Faculty generally have a lot of discretion in determining how best they can add value through their various service activities.  A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H‑1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University–Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H‑1B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Minimum Qualifications: To be eligible to apply for this position, candidates should: Possess a terminal degree (doctorate) in supply chain management or a closely related discipline from a regionally accredited university. Be eligible for the AACSB “scholarly academic” faculty classification (two publications or relevant terminal degree completed since 2022, with viable works in progress). Have a documented track record of successfully teaching supply chain or operations courses, including in fully online formats. Be qualified to teach LSCM 4321, LSCM 4322, and LSCM 4326.   Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate for this position would also possess: At least three (3) years of full-time collegiate teaching experience. Industry experience. Experience developing industry connections in support of academic programs. Proficiency in creating original and engaging online course instructional materials. Qualifications to teach LSCM 4323 and BUSI 3311. Great administrative, organizational, and interpersonal skills to support successful instruction to a largely non-traditional, first-generation, and military-affiliated student body. Familiarity/experience with DBA programs and/or supervision of doctoral students. Salary: Commensurate Hours: Faculty hours; M-F; hours may vary by assignment and course modality. To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Applicants are required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), and either the contact information for three professional references or three letters of recommendation. Additional materials, such as a teaching philosophy statement and transcripts, are optional but strongly encouraged. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
